From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Xun2202 <98207886+Xun2202@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 16:36:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(browse): add swipe modes and resume with softer
 navigation

Shared with Anikku 0101. Increase the adaptive reading shift to 6 percent of viewport, capped at 36dp; deduct the reserved fraction at the same budget scale to remove the near-top dead zone. Lift source filter contents 2dp without changing toolbar bounds. Use a near-critical speed-paced spring and clamp rendered progress, raise intentional reveal travel to 18dp or 24dp while catching a fling, preserving per-touch latch, fast hides and raw scroll velocity. Treat append/loading boundaries as non-terminal until Paging confirms endOfPaginationReached. Add bidirectional popular/latest/filtered content swipes with child-gesture priority, no wrap or offscreen loading, explicit filter snapshots and visited-flow caching; cancelling first filters retains the original list. Add detail left-swipe to latest available history with existing unread fallback, queried asynchronously only on committed gesture, retaining original FAB policy, chapter actions, system back and Anikku player selection. Tests cover gesture boundaries, selection targets, snapshots, folding, header alignment, spring onset and pagination end policy.
